Subject: Allocation-triggered cycle collections run on the young objects only

What this does
  - quickjs.c: JSObject gets a `gc_old` flag (a spare bit of the byte that holds values_inline and has_weak_ref); every creation site clears it. A full collection (gc_scan) sets it on every surviving object.
  - quickjs.c gc_young: a trial deletion (the algorithm of gc_decref / gc_scan / gc_free_cycles) on the set S of heap objects found walking gc_obj_list backwards from its tail until 256 consecutive objects flagged old. Only edges between members of S are removed from the counts, so an object referenced from outside S (an older object, a shape, a closure cell, a register, the native stack) stays alive with everything it reaches. The members left unreached are put on tmp_obj_list and freed by the unchanged gc_free_cycles. Survivors are flagged old.
  - quickjs.c js_gc_auto (used by the allocation threshold and by JS_RunPendingGC; JS_RunGC stays a full collection): a young collection while the heap has not grown more than half past what the last full collection left, a full one at least every 8th collection and when a young one leaves the heap that much larger. QJS_NOYOUNGGC=1 always runs the full one.
  - JSRuntime: three fields appended at the end (gc_young_streak, gc_need_full, gc_full_after).

Why we need it
  The whole-heap trial deletion touches every live object's children on each run; on deltablue gc_scan, gc_decref and gc_free_cycles are 30% of the samples. Garbage cycles are almost always young; the young collection costs what the objects created since the last collection cost, plus one header read per edge from a young object to an older one.

Soundness
  Trial deletion on a subset is sound: the count of every reference from outside the subset is left in place, so a member with a count above zero after the internal edges are removed is held from outside, and the search from those members keeps everything they reach. A cycle that includes an older object, a shape, a closure cell or a bytecode is not found by a young collection (those are never members); the full collection finds it.

Failure modes
  Garbage cycles through older objects or closure cells stay until the next full collection (at most 8 collections later, earlier when the heap grows by half). The member vector and the search stack are static buffers that only grow.

